  "findings": [
    "Original aHash sets bit then shifts on every pixel; with64 inputs drops first decision and always clears lowest bit. High precision256 decisions still returned as u64.",
    "Original dHash resets previous_pixel_value to first_pixel_value instead of current pixel; original module synthetic control13 vs adjacent+wrap9.",
    "All three hash implementations return0 on absent prepared image; error not tagged separately.",
    "Cache keys use full-file SHA1 plus resized dimensions and global version1, without decoder/filter recipe id. Reads entire source into memory.",
    "Cache image decode unwrap and matrix float parse unwrap can panic on malformed readable cache entries; no shape/finite validation.",
    "Cache writes use File::create and write rather than atomic replacement/write_all; invalid metadata can remove configured cache directory recursively. None of those mutation paths executed.",
    "HashType PHash uses DFT real-part mean including DC, not assumed standard DCT median pHash.",
    "Similar() excludes identical original path and fixed perhash radius5; precision not retained in resulting PerceptualHashes."
